\label{th:Ef}
Let  $\sf Gr_{k,n}$ be the Grassmannian of $k$-dimensional vector subspaces of $n$-dimensional space, defined over $\mathbb Z$. 
There exists a tilting vector bundle on  $\sf Gr_{k,n}$ such that its endomorphism algebra has two natural structures of a split quasi--hereditary algebra over $\mathbb Z$.\\

