\label{rem:anti-standard}
The terminology costandard is not used in \cite{WvdK}.  In the usual terminology nowadays, cf.\ \cite[\S 2]{Donsur}, $P(\lambda)$ is the costandard module for $<_e$ with socle ${\sf k}_\lambda$ and $Q(\lambda)$ is the costandard module for $<_a$ with socle ${\sf k}_\lambda$. Dually, $P(\lambda)^*$ is the standard module for $<_a$ with head ${\sf k}_\lambda^*={\sf k}_{-\lambda}$ and $Q(\lambda)^*$ is the standard module for $<_e$ with head ${\sf k}_\lambda^*={\sf k}_{-\lambda}$.
So equation (\ref{eq:P-Q-duality}) is about the interaction of standard and costandard modules for $<_a$, as in \cite[Proposition 3.12]{Ef}.

